# Live Performance Tech Rider and Steps

Technical requirements, stage setup, and quick troubleshooting for a live performance featuring a clarinetist switching between **Roland Aerophone** and **acoustic clarinet**, plus live electronics and visuals.

## Equipment List

### Audio & Instruments
| Item | Specification / Notes |
| --- | --- |
| **Microphone** | DPA 4099 clip-on instrument mic (or equivalent) for acoustic clarinet |
| **Audio Interface** | USB audio interface for laptop / MIDI playback |
| **MIDI Keyboard** | Small 15-key MIDI controller |
| **Mixing Board** | Console with phantom power (+48V) for the DPA 4099 and stereo inputs for Aerophone + interface |
| **Main PA Speakers** | Two speakers in a stereo (L/R) configuration |
| **Monitors** | In-ear monitor (IEM) or on-stage wedge (depending on the musician) |
| **Cables & Adapters** | XLR, TRS/TS instrument cables, USB, and audio/video adapters |

### Stage Furniture, Power & Visuals
| Item | Specification / Notes |
| --- | --- |
| **Performers' Table (Small)** | Holds laptop, audio interface, and 15-key MIDI keyboard |
| **Clarinetist Stand / Table** | Music stand or side table for swapping between Aerophone and acoustic clarinet |
| **Power Strip** | At least 2 outlets near the laptop/interface table |
| **Laptop & Projector** | Laptop running PowerPoint (PPT) connected to venue projector |

## Stage Setup

1. **Place furniture and power:** Set the small table for the laptop, audio interface, and 15-key MIDI keyboard next to the power strip (at least 2 outlets). Place the music stand/swap table within easy reach of the clarinetist.
2. **Connect visuals:** Connect the laptop to the projector and test the PowerPoint (PPT) slides in full-screen mode.
3. **Connect audio to the mixing board:**
   - Clip the **DPA 4099** (or equivalent) onto the clarinet and plug into the mixer with **+48V phantom power** enabled.
   - Connect the **Aerophone** and **audio interface** outputs to stereo/line channels on the mixing board.
   - Plug the **15-key MIDI keyboard** into the laptop via USB.
4. **Set up speakers and monitoring:** Patch the mixing board's **Main L/R** outputs to the two stereo PA speakers, and route a monitor mix to the musician's **in-ear monitor or stage wedge**.
5. **Soundcheck:** Test the Aerophone-to-clarinet swap silently (muting or lowering unused channels if needed) and verify PPT audio/visual cues.

## Quick Troubleshooting

::: tip Problem: No sound from the DPA 4099 clarinet mic
**How to fix it:** Check that **+48V phantom power** is turned on for that mixer channel, verify the microdot-to-XLR adapter is screwed in tightly, and confirm the channel isn't muted.
:::

::: warning Problem: Feedback when switching from Aerophone to acoustic clarinet
**How to fix it:** Point the stage wedge away from the front of the clarinet bell (or switch to in-ear monitors), and roll off low-mid buildup on the clarinet channel EQ.
:::

::: tip Problem: Laptop PPT visuals or MIDI keyboard not responding
**How to fix it:** Check the projector display mode (Extend vs. Duplicate) on the laptop, and plug the 15-key MIDI keyboard directly into a laptop USB port rather than an unpowered hub.
:::
